  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1148 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nOverall, low impact weather is likely through the extended \nperiod. With a slightly colder airmass in place Monday, \ntemperatures will be similar or perhaps a tad cooler than Sunday. \nHowever, low level southerly flow returns to the southern Plains \nby Tuesday as modest upper ridging develops overhead. As a result,\nafternoon temperatures will increase through the end of the week,\nwarming into the upper 80s/lower 90s by late week. Low temps \nlikely end up near or slightly below average Sunday and Monday \nnights (lower-mid 50s) but increase to near or above 60 degrees \nby mid-late week. Dry weather is likely through the forecast \nperiod, though some low rain chances could return by next weekend \nas low pressure lifts north out of TX. This scenario remains \nfairly uncertain as of now, however, and the current forecast \nreflects only low PoPs (<10 percent).",
